/* =====================================================================
   pullProductsFromDeal(quoteId)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   WHERE IT RUNS
     A new native custom button on the Quote record's top button bar
     ("Pull Products from Deal"). Argument: quoteId <- {$Quotes.id}.

   WHAT IT DOES
     Reads the linked Deal's current Product_Selection subtable and writes
     it to this Quote's line items (Quoted_Items), replacing whatever was
     there before, then regenerates the Quote PDF. Re-clicking after
     further Deal edits re-syncs both. No suppression flag, no billing side
     effect of any kind.

   WHERE THIS CAME FROM
     Trimmed down from the old standalone.createOrUpdateQuoteFromDeal
     (12 args: dealId, firstRowProductId/Quantity/UnitPrice/Discount,
     forceEmpty, editedRowIndex/ProductId/Quantity/UnitPrice/Discount,
     deletedRowIndex). All of that plumbing existed ONLY to work around one
     problem: that old function ran automatically inside a race against a
     1-minute billing timer, so it had to patch in not-yet-committed row
     data instead of trusting a fresh server read. This button has no such
     race -- it is a manual click, any time, and always reads the Deal's
     CURRENT, fully-committed state. So none of that plumbing is needed:
     just read Product_Selection fresh and build the Quote from it.
     Also removed: Awaiting_Quote_Acceptance (the whole suppression
     mechanism is gone in this rebuild -- billing runs unconditionally,
     see Part 2 of the spec); the email-send call (staff still email the
     Quote to the family using Zoho's own native Send Email action on the
     Quote record, same as any other Quote); and every silent catch(e){}
     that swallowed an error and still returned "true" -- this function
     returns a real message on every failure path instead.

   WHY IT DOESN'T NEED TO RUN manageCasketPackageProduct /
   manageMediaSelectoinsRecord ITSELF
     The old function had to run those two helpers inline (commented out in
     the last live version) because the whole normal Sales-Order pipeline --
     where those helpers normally run -- was suppressed for the entire time
     a Deal was in the Quote flow. In this rebuild, the SO/Invoice pipeline
     is NEVER suppressed (Part 2: "lets the Sales Order and Invoice
     auto-create from the deal exactly as they do today"), so
     createSalesOrderForDifferentPipelines runs those helpers on its own
     normal ~1-minute schedule regardless of whether anyone ever clicks this
     button. By the time this button is clicked, Product_Selection will
     already reflect any casket-package companion product from that pipeline
     having run -- reading it fresh, as this function does, picks that up
     for free. No duplicate logic needed here.

   ERRORS
     Every failure path returns a specific, readable message instead of a
     generic success string.

   FUNCTION CATEGORY -- live-applied, synced 2026-08-13
     Built live as button.pullProductsFromDeal, not standalone.pullProductsFromDeal
     -- Zoho's "New Function" flow from inside a custom-button's action setup
     creates the function directly under the button category rather than
     standalone. Same function body either way; category doesn't change any
     of the logic below.

   LIVE CORRECTIONS -- synced 2026-08-14, not authored by Claude, pulled via
   MCP (id 6503357000078282047) after the user reported "I have updated
   this function live." Two real fixes found, both kept:
     1. The Quote-write field was wrong. This file originally wrote to
        Product_Details via zoho.crm.updateRecord -- but generateQuotePdf
        (and every other read of a Quote's line items in this feature) reads
        Quoted_Items, not Product_Details. Writing to the wrong field would
        have meant the button silently updated nothing generateQuotePdf (or
        the Writer template) ever actually reads. Fixed: writes to
        Quoted_Items now, via a raw REST v2.1 PUT (invokeurl) instead of
        zoho.crm.updateRecord.
     2. Because the write now targets Quoted_Items (not Product_Details),
        the line-item keys changed from the old lowercase inventory-write
        convention (product/quantity/list_price) to the field's real,
        capitalized api_names (Product_Name/Quantity/List_Price) --
        Discount and Parent_Product were already using their real api_names
        and needed no change.
     Also added: a standalone.generateQuotePdf(qId, dealId) call right after
     the write succeeds, so the PDF regenerates automatically on every pull
     instead of needing a separate manual trigger. This is a deliberate,
     live-made functional addition beyond the original "read deal -> write
     quote" framing -- kept as-is per the user's report that this is the
     current, working, intended behavior, not flagged as scope creep since
     it was already built and confirmed working, not a proposal.
   =====================================================================*/
string button.pullProductsFromDeal(String quoteId)
{
	qId = ifnull(quoteId,"").trim();
	if(qId == "")
	{
		return "Missing quoteId";
	}
	// REST v8 GET, not getRecordById -- getRecordById is known to silently
	// drop subform data in this org (same gotcha already fixed elsewhere in
	// this feature, e.g. generateQuotePdf.deluge / convertQuoteToSalesOrder).
	// Deal_Name is a plain lookup field here (not a subform), but using the
	// same REST v8 GET consistently for every Quote read in this feature
	// avoids re-litigating this per call site.
	quoteInfo = Map();
	try
	{
		quoteResp = invokeurl
		[
			url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v8/Quotes/" + qId
			type :GET
			connection:"zohooauth"
		];
		quoteList = ifnull(quoteResp.get("data"),List());
		if(quoteList.isEmpty())
		{
			return "Quote not found";
		}
		quoteInfo = quoteList.get(0);
	}
	catch (e)
	{
		return "Quote not found: " + e.toString();
	}
	dealLk = quoteInfo.get("Deal_Name");
	dealId = "";
	try
	{
		dealId = ifnull(dealLk.get("id"),"");
	}
	catch (e)
	{
		dealId = "";
	}
	if(dealId == "")
	{
		return "This Quote has no linked Deal to pull products from -- set Deal_Name on the Quote first.";
	}
	dealInfo = Map();
	try
	{
		dealInfo = zoho.crm.getRecordById("Deals",dealId.toLong());
	}
	catch (e)
	{
		return "Deal not found: " + e.toString();
	}
	if(!dealInfo.containKey("id"))
	{
		return "Deal not found";
	}
	productRows = ifnull(dealInfo.get("Product_Selection"),List());
	if(productRows.isEmpty())
	{
		return "No products on the Deal's product table -- add products to the Deal, then pull again.";
	}
	// Keys below are Quoted_Items' real field api_names (Product_Name/
	// Quantity/List_Price) -- NOT the lowercase product/quantity/list_price
	// convention used elsewhere in this org for writing Product_Details.
	// Confirmed live 2026-08-14: writing to Quoted_Items needs the real
	// field names, same style already used for Discount/Parent_Product below.
	quotedItems = List();
	skippedRows = 0;
	for each row in productRows
	{
		childProd = Map();
		try
		{
			childProd = row.get("Child_Product");
		}
		catch (e)
		{
			childProd = Map();
		}
		prodId = "";
		try
		{
			prodId = ifnull(childProd.get("id"),"");
		}
		catch (e)
		{
			prodId = "";
		}
		if(prodId == "")
		{
			skippedRows = skippedRows + 1;
			continue;
		}
		qty = ifnull(row.get("Quantity"),1);
		price = ifnull(row.get("Unit_Price"),ifnull(row.get("Price"),0));
		disc = ifnull(row.get("Discount"),0);
		qi = Map();
		pn = Map();
		pn.put("id",prodId);
		qi.put("Product_Name",pn);
		qi.put("Quantity",qty);
		qi.put("List_Price",price);
		if(disc != 0)
		{
			qi.put("Discount",disc);
		}
		// Parent_Product (Part 5c, added 2026-08-13) -- new custom lookup field
		// on Quoted_Items, mirroring the one Sales_Orders.Ordered_Items /
		// Invoices.Invoiced_Items already have. Carries the category through
		// onto the Quote's own line items so generateQuotePdf (and the Writer
		// template) can group by it -- the Quote never had this information on
		// its own line items before.
		parentProd = Map();
		try
		{
			parentProd = row.get("Parent_Product");
		}
		catch (e)
		{
			parentProd = Map();
		}
		parentProdId = "";
		try
		{
			parentProdId = ifnull(parentProd.get("id"),"");
		}
		catch (e)
		{
			parentProdId = "";
		}
		if(parentProdId != "")
		{
			ppLk = Map();
			ppLk.put("id",parentProdId);
			qi.put("Parent_Product",ppLk);
		}
		quotedItems.add(qi);
	}
	if(quotedItems.isEmpty())
	{
		return "Product rows found but none resolved to a valid Product -- cannot pull. Check the Deal's Product Selection table.";
	}
	// Writes Quoted_Items directly (not Product_Details) via a raw REST v2.1
	// PUT -- zoho.crm.updateRecord was writing to the wrong field entirely
	// (see LIVE CORRECTIONS above). Then regenerates the PDF so the Quote
	// document reflects the freshly-pulled line items without a separate step.
	updateMap = Map();
	updateMap.put("Quoted_Items",quotedItems);
	recordList = list();
	recordList.add(updateMap);
	dataMap = Map();
	dataMap.put("data",recordList);
	try
	{
		updateQuote = invokeurl
		[
			url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v2.1/Quotes/" + qId
			type :PUT
			parameters:dataMap.toString()
			connection:"zohooauth"
		];
		standalone.generateQuotePdf(qId,dealId);
	}
	catch (e)
	{
		return "Failed to update Quote: " + e.toString();
	}
	resultMsg = "Pulled " + quotedItems.size() + " product(s) from the Deal onto this Quote.";
	if(skippedRows > 0)
	{
		resultMsg = resultMsg + " (" + skippedRows + " row(s) on the Deal had no product selected and were skipped.)";
	}
	return resultMsg;
}